Why Is Demand Increasing
Expansion of Therapeutic Applications: Radiopharmaceutical use is moving beyond traditional diagnostic imaging toward targeted therapies, particularly for oncology applications involving therapeutic radioisotopes.
Growth of Targeted Radionuclide Therapy: Lutetium-177 and Actinium-225-based approaches are supporting the development of targeted treatments for cancers and other specialized indications.
Advances in Radioisotope Production: Investment in cyclotron-based, reactor-based, and other isotope-production technologies is supporting supply diversification and the development of new radiopharmaceutical products.

Radiopharmaceutical Watch: Theranostics
Theranostic approaches are becoming an important area of innovation by combining diagnostic imaging with targeted treatment. Radiopharmaceutical pairs can help identify patients with specific molecular targets and subsequently deliver therapeutic radioisotopes to those targets, supporting more personalized nuclear medicine pathways.

