Why This Market Matters
Radiopharmaceuticals are specialized radioactive compounds used for both diagnostic imaging and therapeutic applications in nuclear medicine. Their increasing role in oncology, cardiovascular care, and other clinical areas is creating opportunities for radioisotope producers, pharmaceutical companies, healthcare providers, and technology developers. The market is also being shaped by supply-chain requirements, specialized production infrastructure, regulatory standards, and advances in precision medicine.

